functor: 1
title: not
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`not` · strike · negation.

# Form

`x.not` on a symbol, `(a + b).not` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `in.not` | $in.not$ | font glyph U+2209 |
| `eq.not` | $eq.not$ | font glyph U+2260 |
| `exists.not` | $exists.not$ | font glyph U+2204 |
| `sim.not` | $sim.not$ | font glyph U+2241 |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | Negation. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A line through the base. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.

# From LaTeX

`\notin` becomes `in.not`, `\neq` becomes `eq.not`, `\nexists` becomes `exists.not`.

